      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The paper extends the noncompact gNB converse by splitting the Mellin integral at an adaptive cutoff: ordinary gNB error controls the lower range, while event decomposition, random-dilation moments, and coefficient-weighted rare-tail probabilities control the upper range instead of discarding it.",
